  "prefLabel": "Lot 7202.43 Wide-area progressive link",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Lot 7202.43 “Wide-area progressive link” means “wide-area progressive link” as defined in RSA 287-D:1, XV, namely “a networked gaming system that connects EGDs, including VLTs and HHR machines authorized by RSA 284:22-b, located at multiple licensed gaming establishments to a common progressive jackpot pool, allowing contributions from each linked machine, regardless of location, to incrementally increase a shared jackpot prize, which can be won by any eligible player participating on any of the linked devices.” Wide-area progressive links refers only to wide-area progressive links utilized between gaming establishments located in New Hampshire.\n\nSource. #14341, EMERGENCY, eff 8-21-25; ss by #14503, eff 2-4-26, EXPIRES: 2-4-36 (formerly Lot 7202.31)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/lot7200.html"
